// Ch15 camp (optional, a Hollowmere deck at night; requires ch15_kerrid_revealed). Toma and Kerrid, two soldiers. Toma
// asks the question nobody else will: when no one is still below, does Kerrid go? Kerrid's answer is a watchman's: he
// wants to be relieved. The cost of ending a cycle, for him, is himself (pillar 6), and he wants it. Kerrid's
// post-reveal voice: short, plain, no rank. Nothing of how the dead lift (Act III). Sets ch15_camp_talk.
title: ch15_camp_the_bottom_step
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
Toma [neutral]: Fourteen years on that stair. #line:ch15_camp_001
Kerrid [neutral]: And since. #line:ch15_camp_002
Toma [neutral]: I stood a watch on the seawall at Haluna once. One night. I counted the hours. #line:ch15_camp_003
Kerrid [neutral]: Everybody counts the first night. #line:ch15_camp_004
Toma [worried]: When it is over. When there is nobody left below. Do you go? #line:ch15_camp_005
Kerrid [neutral]: I expect so. #line:ch15_camp_006
Toma [neutral]: Do you want to? #line:ch15_camp_007
Kerrid [neutral]: I want to be relieved. That's what a watch is for. Somebody comes and takes the step. You go down and sleep. #line:ch15_camp_008 #long
Toma [sad]: Who takes the step? #line:ch15_camp_009
Kerrid [neutral]: I don't know. Somebody always has. #line:ch15_camp_010
Toma [neutral]: Then I will stand it with you. Until then. #line:ch15_camp_011
Kerrid [neutral]: Bottom step's mine. You take the one above. #line:ch15_camp_012
<<set $ch15_camp_talk = true>>
===
